<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Widget increment (0.9.0): metadata for the Tide widget
     (TideWidgetProvider.java), referenced from the <receiver> meta-data in
     AndroidManifest.xml.

     minWidth/minHeight: the brief calls for "a 2x1-ish cell". The standard
     cell-size formula ((70 × n) − 30 dp) gives 110dp × 40dp for a strict
     2×1 — but this widget can render up to four stacked lines (the bold
     trend value, the trend sentence, and up to two daily-shape lines), and
     40dp is nowhere near enough room for that stack even at these small
     text sizes. 180dp × 110dp is a judgment call sized the same way
     Runway's own Prüfung widget's minHeight bump was reasoned about (see
     that app's widget_pruefung_info.xml) — "give every row real room,
     real launcher grids tend to be a bit more generous than the strict
     formula anyway" — not a spec number, and, per this increment's own
     constraint, UNTESTED against a real launcher grid (no Android
     SDK/emulator in this environment).

     updatePeriodMillis: 6 hours, same value and same reasoning as Runway's
     own widgets — Android silently CLAMPS any updatePeriodMillis below 30
     minutes up to 30 minutes regardless of what's declared here, so this
     number is a distant backstop, not the app's real update mechanism.
     src/lib/widgets.ts's refreshWidgets() already pushes an immediate
     redraw the moment a weigh-in, plate, skipped meal, health sync, or
     daily-shape target actually changes — this periodic update exists only
     to eventually self-heal a widget that somehow missed one of those
     explicit pushes (e.g. the app was force-stopped mid-write).

     No previewImage/previewLayout — matching Runway's own Prüfung widget
     exactly (see its widget_pruefung_info.xml's own comment: "acceptable;
     note it"). The widget picker falls back to rendering this
     initialLayout itself when neither is set, which is why
     widget_tide.xml carries realistic static placeholder text rather than
     empty TextViews — that placeholder IS the picker preview. Tide's
     minSdk (26) is below API 31 (previewLayout's floor) anyway, so
     declaring one would only ever take effect on a fraction of Android
     versions this app can even install on.

     android:description (API 31+): a one-line summary shown under
     android:label in the picker on Android 12+; silently ignored on older
     API levels, so no compatibility branch is needed for it. -->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="21600000"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_tide"
    android:description="@string/widget_tide_description"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
